1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,496
Before dawn, 6 June 1944.

2
00:00:05,296 --> 00:00:09,152
Ships left ports all along the south coast of England.

3
00:00:08,952 --> 00:00:15,003
They gathered south of the Isle of Wight: "Piccadilly Circus".

4
00:00:14,803 --> 00:00:18,486
Nearly 7,000 vessels crossed the Channel.

5
00:00:18,386 --> 00:00:24,048
Their targets: five beaches along about 80 km of Normandy.

6
00:00:23,748 --> 00:00:27,402
Utah. Omaha. Gold. Juno. Sword.

7
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:33,702
Near Omaha, US Rangers climbed the 30 m cliffs of Pointe du Hoc.

8
00:00:33,702 --> 00:00:40,766
By nightfall, about 156,000 Allied troops had landed, by sea and air.

9
00:00:40,766 --> 00:00:44,742
The way back into Europe was open.
